<aura:documentation>
	<aura:description>
    <p>Create Offering Form Input BASE Component</p>

    <!-- LAST UPDATED DATE / VERSION -->
    <p>Last Updated: 4/30/2019</p>
    <p>CurrentVersion: 1.01</p>
    <hr/>
    <!-- UPDATE DATE / VERSION WITH ANY UPDATES -->

		<p>This is the base component for the various form inputs.</p>
		<br/>
		<p>See the documentation for <code>MarketplaceCreateProductsForm</code> for more details.</p>
		<br/>
		<p>Input Components extend this component, for example:</p>
<pre>&lt;aura:component extends="c:MarketplaceCreateProductFormInputBase"&gt;

  &lt;aura:attribute name="label" type="string" /&gt;

  &lt;lightning:input aura:id="input"
    label="{!v.label}"
    value="{!v.value}"
    required="{!v.required}"
    /&gt;

&lt;/aura:component&gt;</pre>
		<p>In this case the <code>v.label</code> attribute is added.</p>
		<p>However, <code>v.value</code> and <code>v.required</code> are inherited.</p>

		<p>The following base attributes exist for all inputs:</p>
		<ul>
			<li>type (String)</li>
			<li>name (String)</li>
			<li>required (Boolean)</li>
			<li>errorMessage (String)</li>
			<li>layoutItemSize (Integer)</li>
			<li>layoutItemMediumDeviceSize (Integer)</li>
		</ul>

		<br/>
		<p>NOTE: a helper function <code>helper.updateForm(component)</code> must be called to notify the form of changes.</p>
		<p>This function should be called on init, and any time the input changes, for example:</p>

<pre>doInit : function(component, event, helper) {
	component.set("v.valid", true);
	helper.updateForm(component);
},

handleChange : function(component, event, helper) {
	var valid = component.find("input").reportValidity();
	component.set('v.valid', valid);
	component.set('v.touched', true);
	helper.updateForm(component);
}</pre>

		<p>The component keeps track of its internal state and internal UI.</p>
		<p>When <code>updateForm</code> is called, the form checks inputs and updates its own state and UI (Back/Next buttons etc.)</p>

    <!-- CHANGELOG ADD ANY UPDATES HERE -->
